==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|toucher}}, equivalent to {{af|en|touch|-er}}. The pejorative sense is derived from the sense of "[[touch]]ing" someone for money.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ʌtʃə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[touch]]es.
#* {{RQ:Dickens Bleak House|text=We just twist up Chancery-lane, and cut along Holborn, and there we are in four minutes time, as near as a '''toucher'''.|4|25}}
# {{lb|en|bowls}} A [[ball]] lying in contact with the [[jack]].
# {{lb|en|Geordie|pejorative}} A [[toucha]]; one who tries to get something out of others for nothing in return.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|child toucher}}
* {{l|en|near as a toucher}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=cehortu|Hectour|hectour|retouch}}

==French==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|fr|frk|gmw-pro|gem-pro|ine-pro}}
{{inh+|fr|frm|toucher}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|tochier}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.|*tuccō|*toccāre, *tuccāre|t=to strike; to touch}}, probably of {{der|fr|gem|-}} origin, or onomatopoetic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-toucher.ogg|a=Paris}}
* {{rhymes|fr|e}}
* {{homophones|fr|touchai|touché|touchée|touchées|touchers|touchés|touchez}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# the act of [[touching]] {{qualifier|see below}}
# a way of touching
# the sense of [[touch]], [[tactility]]

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{lb|fr|transitive}} to [[touch]] (physically)
#: {{uxi|fr|Ne me '''touche''' pas !|Don't touch me!}}
# {{lb|fr|transitive}} to [[affect]]
#: {{uxi|fr|La maladie '''touche''' actuellement 2 millions de personnes.|The disease currently affects 2 million people.}}
# {{lb|fr|transitive}} to [[receive]], to [[get]]; to [[earn]] (money)
#: {{syn|fr|gagner}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive}} to [[try]], to [[try out]] {{+obj|fr|:à<something>}}
#: {{uxi|fr|Je n'ai jamais '''touché''' au tabac.|I've never tried tobacco.}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive|informal}} to [[know a thing or two]] {{+obj|fr|:en<about something>}}
#: {{uxi|fr|Ce mec est un ancien critique d'art. Je peux te dire qu'il '''touche''' en peinture!|This guy is a former art critic. Believe me, he knows a thing or two about painting!}}

